       --ssttaatt ssttaatt__ffiillee
              This option causes ppppmmttoommppeegg to append the  statistics  that  it
              write  to  Standard  Output  to the file _s_t_a_t___f_i_l_e as well.  The
              statistics use  the  following  abbreviations:  bits  per  block
              (bpb),  bits  per frame (bpf), seconds per frame (spf), and bits
              per second (bps).

              These statistics include how many I, P, and B frames there were,
              and information about compression and quality.



       --qquuiieett _n_u_m___s_e_c_o_n_d_s
