              every _n_u_m___s_e_c_o_n_d_s seconds (unless the time estimate rises, which
              will  happen  near  the beginning of the run).  A negative value
              tells ppppmmttoommppeegg not to report at all.  0 is the default (reports
              once  after each frame).  Note that the time remaining is an es‐
              timate and does not take into account time to read in frames.


       --rreeaallqquuiieett
               causes ppppmmttoommppeegg to run silently, with the only  screen  output
              being  errors.   Particularly  useful  when  reading  input from
              stdin.  The equivalent of the --qquuiieett common option of most other
              Netpbm programs.



       --nnoo__ffrraammee__ssuummmmaarryy
               This option prevents ppppmmttoommppeegg from printing a summary line for
              each frame


       --ffllooaatt__ddcctt
               forces ppppmmttoommppeegg to use a more accurate, yet more  computation‐
              ally expensive version of the DCT.


