       --ssnnrr   This option causes ppppmmttoommppeegg to include the signal-to-noise  ra‐
              tio in the reported statistics.  Prints SNR (Y U V) and peak SNR
              (Y U V) for each frame.  In summary, prints  averages  of  lumi‐
              nance  only  (Y).   SNR  is defined as 10*log(variance of origi‐
              nal/variance   of   error).    Peak   SNR    is    defined    as
              20*log(255/RMSE).  Note that ppppmmttoommppeegg runs a little slower when
              you use this option.


       --mmssee   This option causes ppppmmttoommppeegg to report the  mean  squared  error
