       Select the sequence with the PPAATTTTEERRNN parameter file statement.

       Since  the last MPEG frame cannot be a B frame (see above), if the pat‐
       tern you specify indicates a B frame for the last movie  frame  of  the
       movie, ppppmmttoommppeegg makes it an I frame instead.

       Before  Netpbm 10.26 (January 2005), ppppmmttoommppeegg instead drops the trail‐
